-- ============================================================
-- Alonecraft 4.61 -- Rogue / Subtlety
--   Heightened Senses -> Fieldcraft
--   Enveloping Shadows -> finisher-driven Slice and Dice + Expose Armor
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md:
--   "Heightened Senses (Renamed to Fieldcraft): Your finishing moves have a
--    10/20% chance per combo point spent to restore health equal to 10% of
--    the damage done."
--   "Enveloping Shadows: Your finishing moves have a 6/12/20% chance per
--    combo point spent to also cast Slice and Dice on yourself and Expose
--    Armor on nearby enemies."
--
--
-- BOTH TALENTS BECOME DUMMIES
--
--   Fieldcraft (30894, 30895) drops MOD_STEALTH_DETECT and the two
--   attacker-hit auras; Enveloping Shadows (31211-31213) drops
--   MOD_AOE_DAMAGE_AVOIDANCE.  Each keeps a single SPELL_AURA_DUMMY whose
--   EffectBasePoints carries the per-rank chance-per-combo-point, which
--   RogueFinishers.cpp reads back with GetAuraEffect(...)->GetAmount().
--   That is the module's usual way of handing a rank number to a script and
--   avoids a spell-ID switch in C++.
--
--     Fieldcraft            9 / 19   -> 10 / 20 % per combo point
--     Enveloping Shadows    5 / 11 / 19 -> 6 / 12 / 20 % per combo point
--
--
-- WHY NOT SPELL_AURA_ADD_TARGET_TRIGGER (109)
--
--   Aura 109 with EffectPointsPerComboPoint is how Relentless Strikes does
--   "chance per combo point" with no script at all, and the engine folds the
--   combo points in at SpellInfo.cpp:454 before they are cleared.  It is the
--   right tool for Enveloping Shadows alone.
--
--   It cannot do Fieldcraft: the triggered spell has no access to the
--   finisher's damage, and "10% of the damage done" needs exactly that.
--   Since one SpellScript on the finishers can serve both talents -- and
--   must exist anyway -- both are done there rather than splitting the
--   mechanism across two implementations.
--
--   The trap that forces the script's shape: combo points are wiped in
--   Spell::_handle_finish_phase (Spell.cpp:4243) before proc handling runs,
--   so anything reading GetComboPoints() from a proc sees 0.  The script
--   captures them in BeforeCast instead.
--
--
-- SCRIPT REGISTRATION
--
--   Registered on every rogue finisher, negative IDs for all ranks:
--   Eviscerate, Rupture, Envenom, Kidney Shot, Slice and Dice, Expose Armor
--   and Deadly Throw.
--
--   Registering on Slice and Dice and Expose Armor is safe despite
--   Enveloping Shadows casting those two: the triggered casts happen after
--   the combo points are spent, so they enter the script with 0 combo
--   points, roll a 0% chance and stop.  The script also refuses to run on
--   triggered casts outright.
--
-- ============================================================


